# Review package: ticket 02, 65bc858..0a80ce6

## Commits
### 0a80ce6
docs(core): add the notification fact to the hook contract

Hooks only observe. Record that a hook's presence never changes which
subscribers wake or when, now that hooked and hookless state share one
set trap, and move the roadmap's verified-at line to that commit.

### c7ce796
fix(state): use one set trap for hooked and hookless state

State created with an onWrite hook took a set path that skipped the
batch fast path. Inside a batch, from outside any effect, it scheduled
per property, so a subscriber of an array that read an unchanged index
did not wake, while the same write on hookless state marked the array
dirty and woke every subscriber once at the batch end.

Keep the hookless notification logic for every state object: batch fast
path, no-subscriber shortcut and per-property schedule outside any
effect, loop check inside an effect. Call onWrite as an observer after
the raw write on every path that changes a value, including the batch
fast path. An equal-value write stays silent on every path.

The outside-effect body moves into performUnbatchedWrite because Biome
rejects the unified trap inline for cognitive complexity.


